WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.170
Amritsar.

2
00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:05.680
A temple stands in the middle of
a pool, reached by a causeway.

3
00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.320
Its floor is lower than
the ground around it,

4
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.340
and it has four doors.

5
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:16.750
Its builder, Guru Arjan, installed the
Sikh scripture at its centre in 1604.

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.550
In 1606, under Emperor Jahangir,
Guru Arjan died in Lahore.

7
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.840
So why did the Guru who built the Golden
Temple die at the hands of an emperor?

8
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.610
In this mission, you'll
weigh up the explanations,

9
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.080
and the sources behind each one.

10
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.630
Then you'll trace the
Gurus to Tegh Bahadur,

11
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.210
and a second death, in Delhi.

12
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.980
Your mission: explain why the Guru who
built the Golden Temple died at the hands

13
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:43.890
of an emperor.
